<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Iacetani</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.) · capital Iaca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Pyrenean people of the Jaca valley in Aragon, whose town Iaca is the ancestor of modern Jaca.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Iacetani lived in the upper valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aragon-river">Aragón</a> river in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, around modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaca">Jaca</a>, from at least the 5th century BCE. Their affiliation is uncertain: they may have been related to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vascones">Vascones</a> or to the Iberian peoples to the south.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> places them in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, and their town <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaca">Iaca</a> later minted coins with an Iberian legend. They lived from herding and farming in the mountain valleys. Nothing reliable is known of their rulers or institutions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They appear among the peoples subdued during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cato-the-elder">Cato</a>'s campaign of 195 BCE, though the reference is disputed. Later they lay within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>, and during the Sertorian war their region was fought over; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaca">Iaca</a> survived as a Roman town and gave its name to Jaca.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 500 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:49.75%;width:6.07%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Iaca</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jacetani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-348&amp;focus=iacetani" aria-label="Iacetani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4667 664 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Iacetani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4987 920L5031 967"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4987 920h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4987 920h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Iaca. <a href="/atlas?year=-348&amp;focus=iacetani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
